      "writtenOn": "2019-07-17T07:39:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Swapping 2. and 3. doesn\u0027t make any difference, since\na. \"ipc_handler\" is in ISR (so does \"ipi_handler\"), so nothing should be preempted in between register clearance and ipi_handler()\nb. ipi_enable_irq() should only be called when it is _not_ in ISR.\n\n\n\nfor 3. and 4., I just want to make sure the bit is cleared only when \"ipi_handler\" is executed.\nSince that we want to prevent AP calling other IPC (e.g. IPC2), and we falsely clear the IPC0 bit. (but this case shouldn\u0027t happen on kukui)",
